ceived_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Fixes #5640\n\nPhase 3 of the home-resolution contract (issue #5762): atlas-search / atlas-core / fleet-search home helpers mapped a missing HOME to the literal relative path \"~\" (and an empty HOME to the empty path), so state/config/token paths resolved relative to the current working directory - probe-verified in issue #5640 (`env -u HOME atlas-search init` exited 0 and created ./~/.local/state/... under the CWD, holding the freshly generated client bearer token).\n\nAll 9 sites from the triage verdict (task 12237) now share one behaviour: empty HOME is treated as unset, and unset/empty HOME fails loudly naming HOME. No home-derived path can resolve CWD-relative; absolute overrides (ATLAS_SEARCH_SERVICE_CONFIG, ATLAS_SEARCH_CLIENT_CONFIG, ATLAS_DB, ATLAS_MODEL_DIR) are untouched.\n\nSites: atlas-search server.rs / fetch_model.rs / service.rs / main.rs, atlas-core turso.rs / local.rs (expanduser), fleet-search client.rs / server.rs / serve.rs.\n\nVerification (laptop, this branch):\n- cargo check -p atlas-search -p atlas-core and -p fleet-search: clean\n- cargo test -p atlas-core -p atlas-search: all suites pass (100 tests, 0 failed)\n- cargo test -p fleet-search: 19 passed, 0 failed\n- Probe: `env -u HOME atlas-search init` and `HOME= atlas-search init` both exit 101 with \"HOME is not set or is empty: atlas-search requires a non-empty HOME...\" and create no ./~ or ./.local directory\n\nQueue: task 13607 (repo-health-code-pilot), lane code-d.\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796771540&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=7842&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F7842&signature=38f8ec56ec8b676ef54a79537ed76dcce13a97b60ba8c406870640811ecf5c16\"